            B.q("sa-m2-40", "sa-high-availability", "A single-region Cosmos DB account must keep serving if one data centre in that region fails, at the lowest cost. What do you configure?", listOf("Add a second region", "Enable availability zone support for the region", "Switch to Strong consistency", "Turn on continuous backup"), setOf(1), "With availability zone support, Cosmos DB keeps replicas of the data in different zones of the region, so it carries on through a zone failure. A second region costs more and is for regional outages.",
                scenario = "Alder Bank's Android budgeting app keeps transaction categories in a single-region Cosmos DB account. The bank accepts downtime only for a full regional outage, not for a data centre failure.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
