            B.q("sa-m2-43", "sa-compute", "A workflow must send a document for a manager's approval, wait up to a week for the answer, then continue, written in C# code. What do you recommend?", listOf("A single Azure Function that sleeps until the reply arrives", "Durable Functions with an orchestrator that waits for an external event", "A Container Apps job", "A VM running a Windows service"), setOf(1), "Durable Functions lets you write long-running workflows as code. An orchestrator function can wait days for an external event, such as an approval, without using compute while it waits, then carry on.",
                scenario = "Elmstead Council's Android planning app lets residents submit applications. Each one needs an officer's approval, which can take up to a week, and the developers want to keep the logic in C#.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
                    0 to "A plain function cannot sleep for a week; it hits its time limit and you pay while it waits.",
