            B.q("sa-m2-50", "sa-app-architecture", "A Bicep deployment must create a resource group's resources, delete any resource that is later removed from the template, and stop anyone deleting the resources by hand. What do you recommend?", listOf("Azure Blueprints", "A deployment stack with resources deleted when unmanaged and deny settings that block deletes", "A template spec on its own", "A Bicep deployment in complete mode with a resource lock"), setOf(1), "A deployment stack manages a set of resources as one unit. It can delete resources dropped from the template, and its deny settings stop people deleting or changing managed resources outside the stack. Blueprints retire in January 2027.",
                scenario = "Fieldmouse builds the API for its Android farming app with Bicep and GitHub Actions. Old resources linger after they leave the template, and an engineer once deleted a queue by hand in production.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
                    0 to "Blueprints retire on 31 January 2027, and Microsoft points to template specs and deployment stacks instead.",
                    2 to "A template spec stores and versions a template. It does not clean up or protect resources.",
